  "summary_en": "South Dakota statute (SL 2024 ch 122) permitting fully autonomous (SAE level 4/5) vehicles on public roads without a human driver, setting minimal risk condition, insurance, registration, owner liability and state preemption of local restrictions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Fully autonomous vehicles may operate without a human driver if they achieve a minimal risk condition and comply with traffic laws.",
   "Engaged automated driving system is deemed driver and operator; violations are imputed to the owner.",
